# The `ui!` macro

`ui! { ... }` parses HTML-like markup and emits `html_rs::Element` builder calls.
The macro must be called as `html_rs::ui` (it generates `::html_rs::...` paths).

## Syntax

```rust
ui! {
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-4 p-8 bg-slate-800 rounded-xl">
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">"Counter: "{count.get()}</p>
        <button class="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 rounded-lg cursor-pointer"
                onclick={move || count.update(|c| *c += 1)}>
            "Count (+)"
        </button>
    </div>
}
```

Rules:

- **Tags**: `<tag>...</tag>`, self-closing `<input ... />`. Root must be a single element.
- **Classes**: `class="..."` (also accepts `className`). Dynamic classes: `class={some_string}`.
- **Text**: prefer **string literals**: `"Counter: "`. Raw unquoted text is parsed
  token-by-token with approximate spacing (only use for single words).
- **Interpolation**: `{expr}` inside a text run → `format!` text node:
  `"Counter: "{count.get()}`. A `{expr}` as a whole child is rendered via the
  `Child` trait: any `Display` type → text; `Element` or `Vec<Element>` → element children
  (this is how dynamic lists are spliced in).
- **Events**: `onclick={move || ...}` (no arg) or `onclick={move |e| ...}` where `e: &PointerEvent`.
  Also: `oninput={|text: &str| ...}`, `onenter={|text: &str| ...}` (fires on Enter key in an `<input>`),
  `onkeydown={|k| ...}` (`k: &KeyEventInfo`, fields: `key`, `ctrl`, `shift`, `alt`, `meta`).
- **Attributes**: `value={expr}` / `value="..."` and `placeholder="..."` (used by `<input>`).
  Anything else is rejected at compile time (no silent attrs).

## Elements with behavior

- `<input>`: gets focus on click (blue focus ring), typing dispatches `oninput` with the
  **full new value**, Enter dispatches `onenter` with the current value. It is a
  *controlled* input: render its value with `value={state.get()}` and set the state in
  `oninput`, or the text won't change.
- `<button>` and everything else: opaque boxes (flex containers) unless given classes.

## Supported Tailwind subset (crates/html_rs_core/src/style.rs)

- Layout (flexbox): `flex`, `flex-row`, `flex-col`, `flex-1`, `flex-grow`, `shrink-0`, `block`,
  `items-{start,center,end,stretch}`, `justify-{start,center,end,between,around,evenly}`,
  `gap-N`, `gap-x-N`, `gap-y-N`, `w-N|w-full|w-auto|w-px`, `h-*` likewise, `min-w-0`, `min-h-0`,
  `p|px|py|pt|pb|pl|pr-N`, `m...-N` + `m-auto`, `overflow-hidden`.
- Layout (CSS Grid): `grid`, `grid-cols-N`, `grid-rows-N` (`repeat(N, minmax(0, 1fr))`),
  `col-span-N`, `row-span-N`, `col-start-N`, `row-start-N`, `grid-flow-{row,col,row-dense,col-dense}`,
  `auto-rows-N`; `gap-*` and `items-*`/`justify-*` apply to grid containers too.
- Visual: `bg-{color}`, `border` / `border-N` / `border-{color}`,
  `rounded` `-sm` `-md` `-lg` `-xl` `-2xl` `-3xl` `-full` `-N`, `opacity-N` (percent).
- Text: `text-{color}`, `text-{xs,sm,base,lg,xl,2xl..7xl}`, `font-{thin..black}`,
  `text-{left,center,right}`, `underline`, `line-through`.
- Interaction: `cursor-pointer`, and **`hover:` prefixed variants** (`hover:bg-blue-500`)
  are supported and applied while the pointer is over the element.
- Colors: the full Tailwind v3 palette for slate, gray, zinc, neutral, stone, red, orange,
  amber, yellow, lime, green, emerald, teal, cyan, sky, blue, indigo, violet, purple,
  fuchsia, pink, rose + `white`, `black`, `transparent`, and `bg-[#0ea5e9]` hex literals.
  Opacity modifiers (`bg-blue-500/50`) are NOT supported.
- Spacing scale: Tailwind's `1` = 4 CSS px (0.25rem). Unscaled numbers (text sizes, radii)
  are their own px values. Everything is multiplied by the window scale factor internally.

When extending the class compiler: add a match arm (or prefix-strip branch) in
`apply()` in `crates/html_rs_core/src/style.rs` and a unit test next to the existing ones.
